// Regression test: `import Module::TypeName;` where TypeName is a REAL
// struct/enum but declared in a DIFFERENT module, not Module, must be
// rejected -- registerOnDemandImports() used to only check the flat,
// module-blind isKnownStruct()/isEnumName() EXISTENCE registry for the
// Symbol/SymbolList forms, so `import mem::List;` (List actually lives in
// `list`, not `mem`) incorrectly satisfied the import just because List
// exists SOMEWHERE in the program. Fixed by checking
// getTypeOwningModule(Name) == SourceModule (ownership), not just
// existence -- the same distinction validateModuleQualifier() already
// made for qualified type annotations.

import list;
import mem::List;

